{"issue": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2663", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2663/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2663/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2663/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2663", "id": 3453237968, "node_id": "I_kwDOBabE0s7N1DrQ", "number": 2663, "title": "Invalid index not handled properly in set_current_mission_item_async, ultimately causing segmentation fault", "user": {"login": "irajkovic", "id": 7659522, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjc2NTk1MjI=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7659522?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic", "html_url": "https://github.com/irajkovic", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 2, "created_at": "2025-09-25T11:41:01Z", "updated_at": "2025-10-01T18:29:16Z", "closed_at": "2025-10-01T18:29:16Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "This is a compound issue that ultimately leads to segmentation fault.\n\n**Main issue**:\nIf `MissionRawImpl::set_current_mission_item` (synchronous) is called with an invalid index, the call will be forwarded to the `set_current_mission_item_async`, which checks for index validity, **but it doesn't handle it**. Instead, it only calls the provided callback (lambda from `set_current_mission_item` with `InvalidArgument`) and **proceeds to call `set_current_item_async`** which will ultimately call the same user callback a second time. \n\n```\nif (index < 0 || index >= _mission_progress.last.total) {\n        _system_impl->call_user_callback([callback]() {\n            if (callback) {\n                callback(MissionRaw::Result::InvalidArgument); // <-- we called the callback first time\n                return; // <-- this return applies to the inner lambda\n            }\n        });\n    // <-- we probably want to return here instead, otherwise, function execution continues below\n    }\n    _system_impl->mission_transfer_client().set_current_item_async(\n        index,\n        _system_impl->get_system_id(),\n        [this, callback](MavlinkMissionTransferClient::Result result) {\n            auto converted_result = convert_result(result);\n            _system_impl->call_user_callback([callback, converted_result]() {\n                if (callback) {\n                    callback(converted_result); // <-- and now we call the same callback again!\n                }\n            });\n        });\n```\n\n**Second issue**\nUser callback defined in `MissionRawImpl::set_current_mission_item` works properly for the first invocation. However, after that, `set_current_mission_item` will return. After that, the callback lambda is invoked the second time. By this time, `prom` local variable was already dropped from stack, but lambda holds a reference to it anyway and tries to set it. This causes segmentation fault.\n\n```\nMissionRaw::Result MissionRawImpl::set_current_mission_item(int index)\n{\n    auto prom = std::promise<MissionRaw::Result>();\n    auto fut = prom.get_future();\n\n    set_current_mission_item_async(\n        index, [&prom](MissionRaw::Result result) { prom.set_value(result); }); // <-- Lambda will use local variables from stack, which is fine as long as function didn't return\n    return fut.get(); // <-- This will only block until the first invocation of the provided lambda callback\n}\n```\n\n**Third issue**\nSince we are invoking callback multiple times, it will try to `set_value` on the promise a second time, which is undefined behavior. Although, the code would crash due to second issue already.", "closed_by": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2663/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2663/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": "completed", "pinned_comment": null}, "comments": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/3334820330", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2663#issuecomment-3334820330", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2663", "id": 3334820330, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s7GxVHq", "user": {"login": "irajkovic", "id": 7659522, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjc2NTk1MjI=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7659522?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic", "html_url": "https://github.com/irajkovic", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/irajkovic/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2025-09-25T15:46:57Z", "updated_at": "2025-09-25T15:46:57Z", "body": "On an unrelated note, could you answer the following related question: Is the user required to call the `start_mission()` after the `set_current_mission_item()` is used (assuming the mission is already in progress)?", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/3334820330/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray":